{"name":"Brown Countdown","hex":"#654321","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"},{"term":"countdown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A count backward in fixed units to the time of some event, especially the launch of a space vehicle.","The acts of preparation carried out during this period."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To count down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/countdown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Countdown","blocks":[{"text":"A countdown is a sequence of backward counting to indicate the time remaining before an event is scheduled to occur. NASA commonly employs the terms \"L-minus\" and \"T-minus\" during the preparation for and anticipation of a rocket launch, and even \"E-minus\" for events that involve spacecraft that are already in space, where the \"T\" could stand for \"Test\" or \"Time\", and the \"E\" stands for \"Encounter\", as with a comet or some other space object, like a spacecraft."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Women_world_cup_2015_countdown.JPG/330px-Women_world_cup_2015_countdown.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Countdown","wikidata":"Q775594"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wiki